# Third Party Dependencies

This directory contains third-party libraries and dependencies used by various projects.

## Purpose

Used to manage external libraries that are not part of the core codebase. This helps keep dependencies organized and makes it easier to track versions and licenses.

The next folders are created at runtime
- **fetch**: Contains downloaded external codebases (generated at build time)
- **stage**: Contains the fakeroot for each individual component (generated at build time)

## Adding New Components

When adding a new component

1. Create a .mk file inside the recipes folder \<component>.mk
2. Add this line at the top of the file oss-build-$(OSS_CONFIG_\<COMPONENT>)+=\<component>. This will tell if this recipe is executed depending on configuration
3. Define the component dependencies (if needed): \<component>.depend:=\<component_a>,\<component_b>...
4. Define the next recipes
    - $(call build_oss,\<component>) Recipe for building the component and copying to 'stage' dir
    - $(call clean_oss,\<component>) Recipe for cleaning the building process
    - $(call distclean_oss,\<copmonent>) Recipe for hard cleaning the files created by the build recipe


## Usage
Create a .config configuration file defining the components to be built OSS_CONFIG_<\COMPONENT>=y
make
